I routinely do L and h, and avoid playing dwarves.  This clears out the
primary short-notice offenders from vanilla, and I can take care of the
rest with the resources I'm not wasting.

Now, it _might_ be interesting if, after genocide, anytime a monster
would be generated that was genoed, some new type of nasty appeared
in its place... say, a "spirit" (since we have ghosts and shades
already).

The spirit would be -very- hard to kill, and could spend its time
harassing the player with small obnoxious attacks of some form -- nothing
close to lethal, of course, as otherwise nobody'd bother to take the
risk of genoing anything.  It would follow the player from level to level
and haunt him... growing stronger as further spirits were generated by
absorbing those spirits and becoming more and more dangerous -- perhaps 
gaining different, more aggravating attacks, and eventually gaining
the ability to harshly affect the player -- ie. paralyzing touch in the
middle of combat that free action only reduced, not negated.

Think like Rodney, but less directly hostile and more meddling.

The biggest problem I see with this is that it might make people simply
avoid genociding anything, and then I've wasted a ton of effort; I might
as well have just taken genocide out of the game.  But I suspect
something like this could be effectively balanced with a bit of work.

I'll ponder it over the next few days and see what I come up with.

